      "x": 0,
      "y": -230,
      "w": 700,
      "text": "WP-D · cacheanalyzer\nStructured-card direction, refined. One answer, then everything else.\n\nSample session: 50 requests over 80 min, model switched opus-5 → sonnet-5 at 09:47 and effort high → medium at 10:05, so it exercises the mid-session hard-reset path. 1h wins by $2.13 (31%)."
    },
    {
      "id": "hierarchy",
      "page": "page-1",
      "x": 1240,
      "y": -230,
      "w": 460,
      "text": "Hierarchy\nThe verdict comes first and is the only dark surface on the page — 62px serif, the delta at 58px in mint. Everything after it sits under a \"Supporting detail\" rule: smaller titles, muted ink, counters down to 18px, and the closing notes drop their cards entirely so they read as footnotes on the ground."
    },
    {
      "id": "resets",
      "page": "page-1",
      "x": 1740,
      "y": -230,
      "w": 460,
      "text": "Mid-session model & effort changes\nSession details flag the fields with a CHANGED badge; the timeline gets a segment strip above it (three cache lifetimes) and solid reset rules through it; a violet panel lists each reset with its cause, request number, and the point that matters — a reset costs the same under either TTL, so it argues for not switching mid-session, not for a TTL."
    },
    {
      "id": "palette-note",
      "page": "page-2",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -230,
      "w": 460,
      "text": "Cooler palette\nSlate-blue surfaces replace the neutral grey, brand moves from a corporate navy to deep teal, and cache expiries are violet rather than amber — so the busiest signal on the results screen stays cool. Amber and red are now reserved for validation warnings and rejected files, where they still mean something."
    },
    {
      "id": "l10n-note",
      "page": "page-2",
      "x": 1120,
      "y": -230,
      "w": 520,
      "text": "Text expansion\nSame screen in German — roughly 30-40% longer strings, plus comma decimals and a trailing currency symbol. Nothing has a fixed-width label column, every button and badge sizes to its content, the verdict is allowed two lines, and no text sits inside a bar. This is a layout stress test, not final translation copy."
    }
  ],
  "launch": { "view": "canvas", "page": "page-1" }
}

